<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ishkhani</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Işhan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ishkhani is a medieval Georgian monastery and cathedral in the historic region of Tao, today the village of İşhan in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/artvin">Artvin</a> Province, north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>. Founded in the 7th century, it was rebuilt in the 9th century and given a new dome in the 11th under Bagratid patronage, and it served as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a>'s seat. It is one of the major monuments of the Tao-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/klarjeti">Klarjeti</a> school of architecture.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ishkhani.jpg" alt="Ishkhani" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Armen Manukov · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ishkhan_Monastery_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
